  @invariant  field re-read via cells[row] each keystroke; undo snapshots drive backspace-restore  @ 1254
  @contract  target, facility and key are remembered at take tier; the rest is per invocation  @ 2152
  @contract  with no target the whole of it is the notation snap  @ 2153
  @contract  the facility reads the target as points of the pitch line or as moves between strands  @ 2154
  @contract  purity is the moves facility's alone: how nearly a spelled interval sounds pure  @ 2155
  @contract  returns the steps whose empty shortlists refused the solve, else nil  @ 2156
  @contract  widen stretches those windows to the nearest points instead, so none refuses  @ 2157
  @contract  selection must be exactly one grid column; multi-col selection is a no-op  @ 2955
  @invariant  a 1-col block stays contiguous when it lands on the destination col  @ 2956
  @contract  cursor follows to the destination column (single event and selection alike)  @ 2957
  @contract  refuse if dest col has any onset in source's row extent (note: note-on; else any event)  @ 2958
  @invariant  source's row extent = selection's [r1,r2] for a block, moved event's onset row for a single  @ 2959
  @invariant  tails (either direction) clipped by tm's tail pass; never block  @ 2960
  @contract  per-frame overlay for the chain the caret addresses: notes to ghost, cells to suppress  @ 3470
  @contract  the gate is fxHostAtCursor -- a cell that runs no chain of its own answers nil  @ 3471
  @contract  the window is the viewport's rows, resolved on the producer's own channel  @ 3472
  @contract  notes[colIndex][row] = tm's record by reference; note columns only; first onset wins  @ 3506
  @contract  values[colIndex][row] = { val }; the producer's claimed targets only  @ 3507
  @contract  hidden[cell] = true for every plain original this chain parked; a host cell never hides  @ 3508
  @invariant  a ghosted row may also carry a real cell; precedence is the draw arm's  @ 3509
  @invariant  the overlay lands in the columns that exist; a claim materialises none of its own  @ 3510
  @contract  reentrancy-guarded; bails on no-take (page shows placeholder)  @ 3998
  @contract  takeChanged=true resets ec and re-reads resolution/length/timeSigs  @ 3999
  @contract  grid + ctx rebuild each call; pushMute at end  @ 4000
  @contract  a column's cells/ghosts carry while its events table + projection epoch are unchanged  @ 4001
  @contract  tv consumes configChanged only for transient-frame release and mute pulse  @ 4331
  @contract  rebuild is driven by tm's 'rebuild' signal — closes the (cm, tm) double-fire race  @ 4332
